# ── Capacitor / Android ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The `android/` project itself IS committed — it carries the app id, the label and the manifest,
# and regenerating it from scratch on another machine would silently change all three. What is
# ignored is everything Gradle derives, plus the two files that are machine- or secret-specific:
#   local.properties  names an SDK path that exists only on the machine that wrote it
#   assets/public     is a copy of `dist`, which is already ignored above
android/local.properties
android/.gradle
android/build
android/app/build
android/app/src/main/assets/public
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/build
*.keystore
*.jks

# The staged APK. Built artefacts are handed out, not committed.
dist-apk
